A⇒B).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060142 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "199ef1bf-29a7-5792-bf23-b4a22e87950a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060142 #edb/ref 1074 "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬(A⇒B)≡¬(¬A∨B)\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬A∨B)≡¬(¬A)∧¬B.\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we reach\n\n$$\nA∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $A∧¬B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
